# The keys that may sign a Just Dashboard release.
#
# This file is compiled into the dashboard. While it names no key (comment
# lines only, as now) releases are not signed and no signature is checked.
# From the first release that ships a key here, an install on that release
# updates only to a tag v<version> that one of these keys has signed, and
# refuses everything else. Turning it on, signing a release and replacing a
# key are described under "Signed releases" in
# docs/internal/backend/databases-proxy-platform.md. Read it first: a release
# that ships a key and is followed by an unsigned one leaves every install
# unable to update from the dashboard.
#
# One key per line, in the form ssh-keygen calls ALLOWED SIGNERS. The
# namespaces option is required, so a key used for something else cannot sign
# a release by accident:
#
#   release@just-dashboard.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nza...
